1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,292
In Indonesia, a small fault on a motorbike or a water pump can cost a day's wage. Repair videos can't see your problem, and they're not in your language.

2
00:00:09,292 --> 00:00:16,184
Take a photo and say what's wrong. This recording runs in demo mode, with labelled stand-in photos.

3
00:00:16,184 --> 00:00:26,484
You watch the agent work: as each stage finishes, its result appears. What Muse Spark saw, the parts SAM 3.1 outlined, then the likely cause.

4
00:00:26,484 --> 00:00:32,104
When the evidence is ambiguous, it asks one short question instead of guessing.

5
00:00:32,104 --> 00:00:41,132
Then the diagnosis: likely causes with confidence, a safety level, tools, time, and the parts cost against the repair-shop price.

6
00:00:41,132 --> 00:00:47,544
The parts are masked and numbered on your own photo by SAM 3.1, not a generic diagram.

7
00:00:47,544 --> 00:00:53,812
Before step one, a short safety checklist. The steps stay locked until you tick every item.

8
00:00:53,812 --> 00:01:07,496
New: the live camera guide. Point the phone and SAM 3.1 outlines the exact part to touch, about once a second, on the live picture. In this demo the camera is Chromium's fake camera playing a stand-in photo.

9
00:01:07,496 --> 00:01:16,740
After each step, Check my step. Muse Spark compares the photo with the expected state. Too dark here, so it asks for the torch instead of guessing.

10
00:01:16,740 --> 00:01:20,740
Retake it, and the step is verified before you move on.

11
00:01:20,740 --> 00:01:28,760
Hands dirty? Go hands-free: each step is read aloud, and the phone listens for lanjut, ulang or cek.

12
00:01:28,760 --> 00:01:37,500
Still broken? Say what happened, and the agent re-plans to the next most likely cause. Plan, act, verify, re-plan.

13
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:46,168
Every decision is on screen: what it saw, why it asked, each photo check, each re-plan, and which Meta model did it.

14
00:01:46,168 --> 00:01:50,636
Tap a line, and it jumps to the exact step that was checked.

15
00:01:50,636 --> 00:02:01,296
And when it's a job for a pro, one tap hands it off: a WhatsApp summary of what was found and tried, a search for the nearest bengkel, and a PDF with a brief for the mechanic.

16
00:02:01,296 --> 00:02:07,108
The PDF report carries the same log, so a mechanic can see what was already tried.

17
00:02:07,108 --> 00:02:14,432
Share the guide, and WhatsApp or X shows a card with your marked photo, the likely cause and the safety level.

18
00:02:14,432 --> 00:02:23,460
It also knows when to say no. A rice cooker that won't heat would mean opening 220 volt internals, so the safety gate stops the guidance.

19
00:02:23,460 --> 00:02:30,088
The whole app runs in Bahasa Indonesia, Javanese and English, with Javanese voice input.

20
00:02:30,088 --> 00:02:39,644
And with one switch, diagnosis and planning run on Muse Spark Open, Meta's open-weights model, on Baseten. The app shows a badge when it does.

21
00:02:39,644 --> 00:02:52,176
Under the hood: Voice Transcribe, Muse Spark to see, reason and check, SAM 3.1 for masks and live tracking, and Muse Image for diagrams. Safety is enforced in code.

22
00:02:52,176 --> 00:02:57,176
Tukang Copilot. Every phone becomes a mechanic's apprentice.
